🔧 Geometry Construction: TwoBranch / ThreeBranch System

This section describes how the 2D embedded boundary (EB) geometry is constructed for the TwoBranch and ThreeBranch systems in this detonation simulation.

📐 Overview

The geometry defines a central detonation duct with upper and lower branches extending vertically from a horizontal channel. These branches are used to control wave interference and detonation behavior.

The geometry is built using AMReX's EB2 API by defining a union of solid box regions. The fluid domain exists wherever solid boundaries are not defined.

🧱 Geometry Parameters (from geo namespace in inputs)
Parameter |	Description
W	| Width of the main duct
H	| Height of the upper branch
L	| Depth of the lower branch
xs	| X-position where the branch region begins
xr	| X-position where the branch region ends
mid	| Thickness of the center wall (between upper/lower branches)
cL	| Retraction distance of mid-wall from the left (creates connection to upper/lower)
cR	| Retraction distance of mid-wall from the right
y_offset (optional)	| Vertical shift of the entire duct (used in ThreeBranch)

These are specified in the inputs file using the prefix geo. (e.g., geo.W = 0.04).

🧰 Geometry Construction Logic (in geometry.cpp)

Each solid region is constructed as a BoxIF, which defines a solid box in the domain. These boxes are combined with EB2::makeUnion(...).

🧩 Components:

- Top and Bottom Caps
  Solid boxes that seal the domain vertically above the upper and below the lower branches.
- Side Walls (Left and Right)
  Solid boxes that extend vertically from the domain edge to the beginning (xs) and end (xr) of the branch region.
- Upper and Lower Branches
  Vertical extensions defined by:
    Upper: y_base_hi to y_base_hi + H
    Lower: y_base_lo - L to y_base_lo
- Center Mid-Wall
  A horizontal wall placed between the upper and lower ducts. Can be retracted from either end (cL, cR) to form connections for wave propagation.

